TaskMesh — Alembic migrations
=============================

Single async-Postgres migration tree. Driven by DATABASE_URL from .env at
the project root.

Common commands
---------------

    # Show current schema head
    alembic heads

    # Apply all pending migrations
    alembic upgrade head

    # Generate a new revision from model diffs (autogenerate)
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

    # Generate a blank revision (manual SQL)
    alembic revision -m "describe the change"

    # Stamp an existing production database at the current head WITHOUT
    # running migrations. Use this once per environment that was previously
    # provisioned by backend/db/session.py::_run_migrations so Alembic
    # tracks its state going forward.
    alembic stamp head

Retiring _run_migrations
------------------------

The legacy `_run_migrations` function in backend/db/session.py is left in
place for one release as a fallback. To retire it:

1. Run `alembic stamp head` against every environment.
2. Confirm `alembic_version.version_num = '0001_baseline'`.
3. Delete the call to `_run_migrations` from `create_tables`.

Until step 1 has been done on every environment, leave both paths active.
The baseline migration is idempotent (`create_all(checkfirst=True)`) so
running both is safe.
